1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,100
Local speech AI keeps private recordings off the cloud—
but large models are slow and memory hungry.

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:09,870
This is Pocket Proof, running on a native Arm64 Apple M5.

3
00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:18,400
The same task takes 2.58 seconds with FP16
and 1.62 with Q4.

4
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:27,240
Q4 finishes first: 1.59× faster, 44% less peak memory,
and a 70% smaller model.

5
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:34,500
This is a timed replay of real sequential measurements—
not fake concurrent telemetry.

6
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:41,540
Same audio, decoder, four CPU threads, and native binary.
The only intended change is FP16 weights to Q4_0.

7
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:49,000
Speed is not enough. The featured clip keeps
an exact normalized transcript.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:56,190
Across 30 measured processes, paired median speedup is 1.55×,
with a 1.49–1.62 bootstrap interval.

9
00:00:56,190 --> 00:01:00,700
Pocket Proof also shows the price:
corpus WER moves from 6.9% to 8.3%.

10
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:05,190
The noisy Apollo clip changes one additional word.

11
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:09,200
Even the experiment that failed stays visible.

12
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:13,320
KleidiAI produced no observed gain here,
so it is evidence—not the headline.

13
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:18,000
Anyone can publish a faster number.
Pocket Proof shows whether you should believe it—

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,210
whether the quality cost is worth shipping, and gives you
every raw run needed to reproduce the decision.
